## Lesson learned

Checks-effects-interactions ordering isn't a style preference -- it's the literal, mechanical thing that determines whether a contract holding real money can be drained in a single transaction. And a test suite that only ever exercises normal wallets, no matter how thorough, will never catch a bug that only a malicious contract can trigger. That's exactly the gap between the clean testnet rehearsal and this exploit -- and it's why this exact test now runs forever, on every future change.
